  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="812cafaf-9aad-552d-a536-adda5e25f42d" activityNameId="1c1d8c8d-5d58-5ede-b8e6-ead7547c8bf5" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Soap, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Soap, at plant
data based on the ECOSOL study of the European surfactant industry. Allocations in multioutput processes were made, using the relative mass outputs of products.;
CAS number: 068952-95-4; 
UUID: a471059f-d4cf-348b-8010-fcfa8ec751f3
This module contains material and energy input, production of waste and emissions for the production of soap out of fatty acids from palm and coconut oil. Transports and infrastructure have been estimated. No water consumption included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Average technology for the production of soap out of a blend of fatty acids from palm and coconut oil, representing typical European production mix in the mid 90s. The ratio of short to long fatty acid chains is 20:80, the moisture 13%.
Time period: data of published literature
Production volume: na
Sampling: data out of ECOSOL study of European Surfactant Industry. Common translation rules used, reported in Chemical report (Althaus et al. 2003). 
Extrapolations: unspecified metal emissions to water omitted.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a471059f-d4cf-348b-8010-fcfa8ec751f3.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
